          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "amita is probably built on a nursery word, Proto-Indo-European amma-, \"mother\" (EtymDB 2.1), with a suffix."
            }
